{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Hear, O Israel.</b> We find in the Aggadah: the ayin of שמע is suspended, because the Holy One, blessed be He, created His works with an ayin-by-ayin progression. How so? Israel is one of the seventy among the nations; the nations are one of the seventy among the beasts; beasts are one of the seventy among the birds; birds are one of the seventy among the fish; fish are one of the seventy among the demons; demons are one of the seventy among the angels. And the Holy One, blessed be He, is King over all of them. Upon this the payytan founded, in the hymn of the first things: 'and His name is exalted above seventy.'" "<b>Hear, O Israel</b> etc. Hear and understand this matter: HaShem who was from eternity at the beginning — He is the HaShem of now, and He is the HaShem who shall live and endure without end or limit. And in this respect He is <b>one</b> — that is, He alone possesses a unity such as has never been and will never be in anything in the world. Another interpretation: it is impossible here with fewer than three mentions, because of the slander of the nations of the world. For if he had said שמע ישראל ה׳ אחד, each and every nation would say it as their reproach against us — that about ours He says He is one. Now that we say אלקינו, it is known that He speaks of the Elohim of Israel, who is with them. And if he had said ה׳ אלקינו אחד, they would say that the Elohim of Israel is one of the elohim. All the more so if he had said שמע ישראל אלקינו אחד."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "The phrase 'with an ayin-by-ayin progression' (בעי״ן עי״ן) is opaque; rendered hyper-literally. The argument appears to concern a chain of diminishing proportions, each a seventieth of the next, associated with the letter ayin (numerical value 70)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:57.482044031Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}